Determine whether the declared parameter qualifies as an 'in-out' parameter
for our purposes: type <a class="external-link" href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/17/docs/api/java.sql/java/sql/DatabaseMetaData.html#procedureColumnInOut" title="class or interface in java.sql"><code>DatabaseMetaData.procedureColumnInOut</code></a>,
or in case of a function, <a class="external-link" href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/17/docs/api/java.sql/java/sql/DatabaseMetaData.html#functionColumnInOut" title="class or interface in java.sql"><code>DatabaseMetaData.functionColumnInOut</code></a>.

Determine whether the declared parameter qualifies as an 'out' parameter
for our purposes: type <a class="external-link" href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/17/docs/api/java.sql/java/sql/DatabaseMetaData.html#procedureColumnOut" title="class or interface in java.sql"><code>DatabaseMetaData.procedureColumnOut</code></a>,
or in case of a function, <a class="external-link" href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/17/docs/api/java.sql/java/sql/DatabaseMetaData.html#functionColumnOut" title="class or interface in java.sql"><code>DatabaseMetaData.functionColumnOut</code></a>.
